e and I reminded myself how much I  wanted it and then I sat down and I just  started doing  I started writing words and maybe  they're not that great and I'll edit  them later but just the fact that like  you just have to start doing you know  you can talk talk talk at the end of the  day just visualize your goal chunk it  out into you know actual tasks set  metrics to to show that you're making  progress and then just that's cool I'm  looking forward to seeing the book too  man that's exciting I'm excited one of  my favorite bits of advice is from  Michael Dell who talked about  understanding your point of leverage and  one of the things that I constantly try  to think about for myself is what's the  best use of my time to drive the needle  as far as i can forward so you know even  a task is of 100 things plus you're  behind you know you feel in your life  and you catch up on your bills and wants  for town with your your wife there's a  lot of things on your plate so you only  have a certain amount of time to be able  to focus on this new thing what activity  or you great at that you can really  spend energy on that's really going to  move it forward so yes you have your  goals you have your vision you have your  plan and then look at that task list and  which one that if you attack today  that's going to help really move your  project forward because it's leveraging  what you're passionate about what you've  got you know your break skills at I feel  like if people understood their point of  leverage a lot better than you be able  to make faster growth and catch up and  get to where you want to go a lot sooner
 

